--- !u!114 &602905744
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 602905740}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e902414e3c2f1f8409f768501993574f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PatchNotesView
  notesText: {fileID: 1239978752}
  patchNotes: "1.0.6\n- \u201CNext shadow\u201D button now reveals the next Pok\xE9mon
    silhouette in Pok\xE9dex order \n- Reduced empty space between the main title
    and the first generation (Kanto)\n- Finished dialog now shows how many type hints
    and shadows were used\n- Green / red result borders now work correctly again
    after using Give up\n- Reduced Pok\xE9mon sprite resolution from 512\xD7512 to
    128\xD7128, resulting in shorter loading times and a significantly smaller game
    size\n\n1.0.5\n- Improved quiz layout: all section titles are now left-aligned
    and automatically scale with the grid size for better readability\n- Added Patch
    Notes History, accessible from the main menu\n- Added Pok\xE9mon silhouette mode
    (\u201CShadows\u201D), allowing players to reveal shadow versions of all Pok\xE9mon\n\n1.0.4\n-
    Tooltip for patch notes no longer overflows the right side of the screen when
    the text is long.\n- No need to type \u201CAlolan\u201D, \u201CGalarian\u201D,
    or \u201CHisui\u201D in Gen 7/8 quizzes if the base form exists in earlier generations.\n-
    All Pok\xE9mon should now appear in the correct order in every quiz.\n- Type
    quizzes now use the same background color as their corresponding type buttons.\n-
    Added Lumiose Mega Evolutions.\n- Meltan and Melmetal appear in the Unknown section
    under Alola, matching the original quiz. \n- Mega Evolutions are now split into
    \u201CMega Evolution \u2013 Kalos\u201D and \u201CMega Evolution \u2013 Hoenn\u201D.\n\n1.0.3\n-
    Re-typing a Pok\xE9mon name now clears the input field and plays the duplicate-guess
    sound. \n- Added a Pause Menu: pressing Esc (or the Pause button) pauses the
    quiz, hides the grid, and shows total elapsed time with a Resume button. \n-
    Fixed an issue where correct/incorrect outline colors after Give Up did not scale
    properly with different grid sizes.\n\n1.0.2\r\n- Added a Card Size slider allowing
    you to adjust Pok\xE9mon tile size (zoom in/out).\n\n1.0.1\n- The game can now
    automatically check for and download updates. \n- Added a toggle to always scroll
    to the entered Pok\xE9mon, even if it was already guessed.\n- After pressing
    Give Up, guessed Pok\xE9mon display a green outline and missed ones show a red
    circle.\n- The final results dialog now has a Close (\xD7) button and stays open
    until manually dismissed.\n- Added a toggle + slider for background music, with
    volume preserved between scenes.\n- Added distinct sound effects for correct
    guesses and duplicate guesses. \n- Buttons now have mouse hover animations.\n-
    The PC executable now uses a Pok\xE9 Ball icon."
